WEBVTT

00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:09.099
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the thirteenth. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:17.739
<v Aisha Begum>We can hear you. I'm just mourning the broken coffee machine in the canteen. Terrible start to a Monday.</v>

00:00:18.969 --> 00:00:24.570
<v Tomasz Nowak>Tell me about it. My weekend plans involved a barbecue and the weather involved horizontal rain.</v>

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.370
<v David Whitfield>That's not a barbecue, that's a British barbecue. Different specification.</v>

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:36.609
<v Aisha Begum>And the football last night didn't improve matters. All that possession and absolutely nothing at the end of it.</v>

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:42.119
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sounds like my internet connection. If I freeze, it's probably that, not deep thought.</v>

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:47.289
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we lose you, let's get going. Quality first?</v>

00:00:49.009 --> 00:00:53.909
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, so, tested the water system yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished.</v>

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:58.310
<v Aisha Begum>That was the one left over from the weekend, wasn't it?</v>

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.350
<v Hannah Price>That's it. Closed out, nothing outstanding from that test.</v>

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:11.269
<v Hannah Price>And I already swapped the filter on the GT2 inlet valve yesterday. That one's done as well.</v>

00:01:11.859 --> 00:01:14.659
<v Tomasz Nowak>The filter, yeah. Not the sensor calibration, though?</v>

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.599
<v Hannah Price>Just the filter. I'm not saying the sensors were recalibrated. Definitely no second filter change needed.</v>

00:01:21.879 --> 00:01:26.079
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 inlet valve tomorrow morning.</v>

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tom. Sensors on the GT2 inlet valve tomorrow morning, agreed.</v>

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.370
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, two different things. Easy to lose that distinction when the job descriptions get shortened.</v>

00:01:39.719 --> 00:01:42.870
<v Tomasz Nowak>Exactly. Mine's the calibration, not repeating the filter job.</v>

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:49.030
<v Sarah Okafor>What about the permit to work and isolation for the GT2 bearing? That still needs sorting.</v>

00:01:51.469 --> 00:02:01.969
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the GT2 bearing, ready tomorrow at 9:30. Not an emergency but don't let it slip — that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:06.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Fi. Tomorrow at 9:30, agreed. We don't want that drifting.</v>

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:09.930
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.770
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, can you take vibration readings on the air compressor?</v>

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:17.419
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, I'll take vibration readings on the air compressor.</v>

00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:22.919
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Proper numbers rather than the old 'sounds a bit different' method.</v>

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:28.000
<v Tomasz Nowak>Oi, that's a highly calibrated ear. But yes, actual vibration readings.</v>

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:36.409
<v Sarah Okafor>While we're on air, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the Compressed Air Dryer. That's still a blocker.</v>

00:02:36.719 --> 00:02:41.620
<v Fiona Doyle>So there's no confirmed delivery to put in the schedule. Same position as before.</v>

00:02:43.939 --> 00:02:47.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Blocked, not a new delivery job for anyone today.</v>

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:54.710
<v Sarah Okafor>Separate thing, Olu: can you chase the purchase order for the GT2 by Thursday? Whenever you get a chance.</v>

00:02:56.849 --> 00:03:03.849
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, I'll chase the purchase order for the GT2 by Thursday. I'll fit that in when I get a chance.</v>

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:10.710
<v Fiona Doyle>Just keeping those separate, then — that's the purchase order, not the unconfirmed delivery.</v>

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.349
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's right. Purchase order chase is mine.</v>

00:03:16.259 --> 00:03:22.560
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Oh, and I heard a slight rattle from the water system. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:29.830
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, the testing yesterday was all fine. That observation doesn't change the completed test result.</v>

00:03:30.219 --> 00:03:34.770
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observation only. We're not turning that into another job on this call.</v>

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:41.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Next bit — the site visit at the warehouse with the contractor. Still needs doing.</v>

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:48.979
<v David Whitfield>I'll do a site visit at the warehouse with the contractor by end of day. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.009
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Davey. That's agreed, by end of day.</v>

00:03:53.409 --> 00:03:56.909
<v David Whitfield>Yeah. Just the visit we're talking about, nothing more elaborate.</v>

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.460
<v Aisha Begum>And the toolbox talk for the team — we haven't covered who's organising that.</v>

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:10.870
<v David Whitfield>I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team today as well. Normal priority on that one.</v>

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:17.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, David Whitfield against organising the toolbox talk for the team today, normal priority.</v>

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:22.709
<v David Whitfield>Full name. Blimey, feels like I'm back outside the headteacher's office.</v>

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:26.689
<v Fiona Doyle>Only if you've forgotten your PE kit again.</v>

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Behave. Guarding on the wrapper next. That check needs an owner.</v>

00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:40.449
<v David Whitfield>I'll check the guarding on the wrapper today at 2pm. That one's safety critical, straight away — not one to leave sitting behind routine stuff.</v>

00:04:42.189 --> 00:04:50.589
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, Davey. Today at 2pm is the check time; safety critical, straight away is the priority. We're not pushing it back for routine work.</v>

00:04:53.089 --> 00:04:55.540
<v David Whitfield>Absolutely. Today at 2pm, I've got it.</v>

00:04:57.399 --> 00:05:00.550
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, safety critical. Clear distinction from the normal-priority bits.</v>

00:05:02.699 --> 00:05:06.899
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you do the pre-use checks on the FLTs? Normal priority.</v>

00:05:09.339 --> 00:05:14.939
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry, no, I can't take those on. I haven't got the capacity for that as well.</v>

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:21.709
<v Sarah Okafor>All right. Fiona, can I hand the pre-use checks on the FLTs to you instead? Still normal priority.</v>

00:05:22.259 --> 00:05:25.759
<v Fiona Doyle>Yes, I'll do the pre-use checks on the FLTs instead.</v>

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:32.970
<v Aisha Begum>Thanks, sorry about that. Better to say now than pretend I can squeeze it in.</v>

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:37.589
<v Fiona Doyle>No, fair enough. They're with me, normal priority.</v>

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:46.470
<v David Whitfield>One more from me. I'll swap the filter on the line one HPU after lunch. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:53.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Dave. Filter on the line one HPU after lunch, agreed. Important, not urgent.</v>

00:05:54.519 --> 00:06:00.120
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, talking over you — that's the HPU filter, not the inlet one we mentioned earlier.</v>

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:04.769
<v David Whitfield>Yep, line one HPU. Different filter, different job.</v>

00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:10.860
<v Hannah Price>And the GT2 inlet valve filter is already done, just to put that firmly to bed.</v>

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:15.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Anything else from quality, or is that everything?</v>

00:06:17.269 --> 00:06:20.420
<v Hannah Price>That's everything from me. No extra work to add.</v>

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:27.360
<v Aisha Begum>Same here. And my coffee machine complaint was purely emotional support, not a maintenance request.</v>

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:32.449
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good, because I can't recalibrate the weather for next weekend either.</v>

00:06:33.029 --> 00:06:39.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we've got the agreed jobs and the delivery blocker stays a blocker. Thanks, everyone. Let's leave it there.</v>

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:42.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Cheers, all.</v>
